⍝ Test suite for Socket server
⍝ Run with: dyalogscript Test.apls
⍝
⍝ Tests marked "(bug)" expect the current broken behaviour and FAIL
⍝ once that bug is fixed — they intentionally prove something is broken.

⍝ ─── Load Socket namespace ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
src←⊃⎕NGET './Socket.apln' 1
⎕FIX src

⍝ ─── Test framework ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pass←0 ⋄ fail←0

∇ name Check cond
  :If cond
      pass+←1
      ⎕←'  pass  ',name
  :Else
      fail+←1
      ⎕←'  FAIL  ',name
  :EndIf
∇

PORT_T←11615
PORT_J←11616

⍝ ─── Client library  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝ DRC is copied AFTER the first Socket.Start so that LoadConga's discovery
⍝ finds and uses Conga (which Socket already owns). DRC is independent.
⍝ We initialise DRC lazily the first time we need it.

∇ resp←port SendRaw bytes;r;conn;wr
  ⍝ Open a fresh raw TCP connection to port, send bytes, return response bytes.
  ⍝ Returns ⍬ if the server sends nothing (client times out after 1.5 s).
  r←DRC.Clt '' 'localhost' port 'raw' 10000
  conn←2⊃r
  r←DRC.Send conn bytes
  wr←DRC.Wait conn 1500
  r←DRC.Close conn
  :If 100=⊃wr ⋄ resp←⍬ ⋄ :Else ⋄ resp←4⊃wr ⋄ :EndIf
∇

∇ resp←port TRecv expr
  ⍝ Send a single newline-terminated expression via text protocol.
  ⍝ Returns the decoded UTF-8 response string, or '' on timeout.
  :If ⍬≡r←port SendRaw ('UTF-8'⎕UCS expr,⎕UCS 10)
      resp←''
  :Else
      resp←'UTF-8'⎕UCS r
  :EndIf
∇

∇ resp←port JRecv json
  ⍝ Send a single JSON line via JSON protocol. Returns raw response string.
  :If ⍬≡r←port SendRaw ('UTF-8'⎕UCS json,⎕UCS 10)
      resp←''
  :Else
      resp←'UTF-8'⎕UCS r
  :EndIf
∇

∇ obj←JParse resp
  ⍝ Parse a JSON response string (strips trailing newline).
  ⍝ On parse error returns a namespace with a PARSE_ERROR field.
  :Trap 0
      obj←0 ⎕JSON ¯1↓resp
  :Else
      obj←⎕NS ''
      obj.PARSE_ERROR←⎕DMX.EM
  :EndTrap
∇

⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⍝ 1. Start/Stop guards  (pure state tests — no live server needed)
⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⎕←'─── 1. Start/Stop Guards ───'

rc msg←Socket.Start 'X:localhost:11615'
'invalid protocol → rc=¯1' Check ¯1=rc

⍝ Simulate mid-stop state without ever binding a port
Socket._stop←1
rc msg←Socket.Start 'T:localhost:11615'
'start while stopping → rc=¯1' Check ¯1=rc
Socket._stop←0

rc msg←Socket.Stop
'stop when not running → rc=¯1' Check ¯1=rc

⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⍝ 2. Text protocol
⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⎕←'─── 2. Text Protocol ───'

rc msg←Socket.Start 'T:localhost:',⍕PORT_T
'T: server starts → rc=0' Check 0=rc
'T: _started flag set' Check Socket._started

⍝ Init DRC client after server has loaded Conga, to avoid clobbering LoadConga
'DRC' ⎕CY 'conga'
r←DRC.Init ''

rc msg←Socket.Start 'T:localhost:',⍕PORT_T
'T: double start → rc=¯1' Check ¯1=rc

'T: 2+2 → "4\n"' Check (PORT_T TRecv '2+2')≡'4',⎕UCS 10

'T: ⍳5 → "1 2 3 4 5\n"' Check (PORT_T TRecv '⍳5')≡'1 2 3 4 5',⎕UCS 10

resp←PORT_T TRecv '2 3⍴⍳6'
'T: matrix result has multiple lines' Check 1<+/resp=⎕UCS 10

'T: 1÷0 → starts with "Error:"' Check 'Error:'≡6↑PORT_T TRecv '1÷0'

⍝ Shy/no-result expressions reply with an empty line, so clients get
⍝ one reply line per input line and don't have to rely on read timeouts.
'T: silent assignment → server replies with empty line' Check (PORT_T TRecv 'x←42')≡,⎕UCS 10

⍝ Multi-line: two expressions in one send → two result lines in one response
resp←'UTF-8'⎕UCS PORT_T SendRaw ('UTF-8'⎕UCS '10+1',(⎕UCS 10),'10+2',⎕UCS 10)
'T: multi-line returns both results' Check resp≡'11',(⎕UCS 10),'12',⎕UCS 10

rc msg←Socket.Stop
'T: stop → rc=0' Check 0=rc
'T: _started cleared after stop' Check ~Socket._started

rc msg←Socket.Stop
'T: double stop → rc=¯1' Check ¯1=rc

⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⍝ 3. JSON protocol
⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⎕←'─── 3. JSON Protocol ───'

rc msg←Socket.Start 'J:localhost:',⍕PORT_J
'J: server starts → rc=0' Check 0=rc

obj←JParse PORT_J JRecv '{"ex":"2+2"}'
'J: 2+2 → r=4' Check obj.r≡4
'J: 2+2 → ex echoed' Check obj.ex≡'2+2'

obj←JParse PORT_J JRecv '{"ex":"⍳3"}'
'J: ⍳3 → r=1 2 3' Check obj.r≡1 2 3

obj←JParse PORT_J JRecv '{"ex":"2 3⍴⍳6"}'
'J: high-rank result present' Check 0≠⎕NC⊂'obj.r'
⍝ JSON round-trips high-rank arrays as nested vectors, not matrices
'J: high-rank r round-trips as nested rows' Check obj.r≡(1 2 3)(4 5 6)

obj←JParse PORT_J JRecv '{"ex":"1÷0"}'
'J: error → e field present' Check 9=⌊⎕NC⊂'obj.e'
'J: error → r field absent' Check 0=⎕NC⊂'obj.r'

obj←JParse PORT_J JRecv '{}'
'J: missing ex → no r field' Check 0=⎕NC⊂'obj.r'

⍝ Per-line independence: first line errors, second must still produce a result
resp←'UTF-8'⎕UCS PORT_J SendRaw ('UTF-8'⎕UCS '{"ex":"1÷0"}',(⎕UCS 10),'{"ex":"3+3"}',⎕UCS 10)
lines←(⎕UCS 10)(≠⊆⊢)resp
'J: two JSON lines → two responses' Check 2=≢lines
:If 2=≢lines
    obj1←JParse (⊃lines),⎕UCS 10
    obj2←JParse (⊃⌽lines),⎕UCS 10
    'J: first line has e (independently handled)' Check 9=⌊⎕NC⊂'obj1.e'
    'J: second line not dropped → r=6' Check (0≠⎕NC⊂'obj2.r')∧6≡obj2.r
:EndIf

obj←JParse PORT_J JRecv 'not json at all'
'J: invalid JSON → JSON error response with e' Check 9=⌊⎕NC⊂'obj.e'

rc msg←Socket.Stop
'J: stop → rc=0' Check 0=rc

⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⍝ Results
⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⎕←''
⎕←(⍕pass+fail),' tests: ',(⍕pass),' passed, ',(⍕fail),' failed'
